      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. i'll run it through the scanner to see how the score looks. \n\nactually, looking back at it, some of those sentences feel a little forced, like where you mentioned python and cloud architecture. it's okay if it's a bit dense, but i'm worried if a human recruiter reads it, they'll immediately notice it's just a list of buzzwords in disguise. \n\ncan you try one more version? try to weave them in even more deeply so the 'Term Coverage' score stays high, but make it feel more like a cohesive story of their career rather than just hitting every point in a sequence. please don't just add the words at the end in a block or weirdly break the sentences just to fit them in, we really need to keep the professional tone intact.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
